# Settings of massimo serve, read by the service with -env (see README.md
# and packaging/README.md). Readable only by the user _massimo.
#
# Per Cube (the serial as printed on it):
# MASSIMO_CUBE_<SN>_ADDRESS=192.168.1.10
# MASSIMO_CUBE_<SN>_KEY=...
# MASSIMO_CUBE_<SN>_IV=...
# MASSIMO_CUBE_<SN>_PROXY=<an address of this box, one per Cube>
#
# serve keeps the Cubes in its store, massimo.db in the data directory:
# at its first start it adds every Cube of this file, and from then on
# the store wins. _ADDRESS, _NAME, _PROXY, _PROXY_SERIAL and _IGNORE here
# only add a Cube the store does not know yet; a line that differs from
# the store is logged at the start. Change a known Cube in the web UI,
# Settings → Cubes. _KEY and _IV are read from here only.
#
# The owner's key, made at the first start (README.md, "Server"); a user
# made with massimo user add or in the web UI closes the API as well.
# Until one of them is there, every device on the local network may use
# the server:
# MASSIMO_API_TOKEN=...
#
# Lets the owner reboot this computer from the web UI (System settings →
# Maintenance); Linux and macOS also need the root helper of
# `sudo massimo install -reboot-helper`. on, true, yes, 1 or enabled
# switch it on, off, false, no, 0, disabled or nothing off, in any case:
# MASSIMO_REBOOT=on
#
# serve announces itself on the LAN by mDNS (UDP 5353) as _massimo._tcp,
# for massimo discover and the apps, when it listens on an address the
# LAN reaches; off stops it, with the same values as MASSIMO_REBOOT:
# MASSIMO_ANNOUNCE=off
MASSIMO_LOG=/var/log/massimo/serve.log
